.TH UH7000-PIPEWIRE 1 "July 2026" "tascam-uh7000-linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uh7000-pipewire \- expose UH-7000 analog playback as a PipeWire sink
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uh7000-pipewire
.RB { enable | disable | set-default | status }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uh7000-pipewire
creates the per-user PipeWire-Pulse virtual sink
.B uh7000-analog
and directs its stereo 48 kHz S24_3LE PCM FIFO to
.BR uh7000-stream (1).
The hardware remains in vendor configuration 1 while the sink is active.
.B disable
stops the stream and returns the device to its normal USB Audio 2.0
configuration 2 card.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B enable
Create the virtual sink and start the stream service. The default desktop sink
is not changed.
.TP
.B set-default
Enable the sink and select it as the current PipeWire-Pulse default.
.TP
.B disable
Remove the virtual sink and stop the configuration-1 stream.
.TP
.B status
Report whether both the sink and stream service are active.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires a running PipeWire-Pulse session and the
.B pactl
utility. The package recommends
.B pipewire-pulse
and
.BR pulseaudio-utils .
.SH SAFETY
The normal configuration-2 control service remains available for read-only
state while the stream is active, but switching clock source or using the UAC2
card should be done only after disabling the analog sink. Disconnect speakers
and headphones before diagnostic tones or first-use routing checks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uh7000-stream (1),
.BR uh7000ctl (1)
